cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Who pays the token tax? Fertility or accounting in the quality penalty of high-fertility languages"
abstract: >-
  A preregistered study that separates tokenizer fertility from token-denominated accounting,
  within each of five languages at fixed text. For a 17M-parameter model at 2.25x fertility,
  counting the training budget and the context window in content removes 75% of the
  bits-per-byte penalty (95% CI 69-89%); a content-matched residual of 0.039 bits per byte
  (95% CI 0.007-0.070) remains.
